# trivy vulnerability ignore-list — the ONLY sanctioned way to accept a HIGH/CRITICAL
# finding in a shipped image. Both gates read this file:
#   - CI:    .github/workflows/images.yml — always THIS file as of the workflow's own commit (also
#            when a manual run re-publishes an older tag), checked out to .cve-policy/
#   - local: scripts/images/sbom-scan.sh  (--ignorefile <repo>/.trivyignore)
#
# POLICY (see scripts/images/RUNBOOK.md "Base-image policy"):
#   1. Prefer to FIX: bump the distroless base digest to a patched build, or drop the
#      offending package. The images are distroless — the OS surface is ~10 packages,
#      so genuinely-unfixable HIGH/CRIT is rare.
#   2. Only when a CVE is non-applicable or upstream has no fix, add it HERE with:
#        - the CVE id
#        - a one-line justification (why it's non-exploitable / unfixable in our use)
#        - a date + optional expiry so it gets re-reviewed.
#
# Format: one `CVE-XXXX-YYYY` per line. Example (kept as a template, NOT active):
#   # CVE-2023-45853  zlib MiniZip — not compiled into Debian's zlib; unreachable.
#   #                 (would only appear on a base that ships zlib1g; distroless/cc does not)
#
# Add entries only with justification. `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` makes trivy report the CVE again
# after that date, which forces the re-review.

# libssl3 3.0.20 (distroless/cc-debian12 base) — DTLS handshake-retransmission info disclosure.
# NOT APPLICABLE: no shipped binary links OpenSSL (TLS is rustls + ring/aws-lc-rs, statically
# compiled; `cargo tree -i openssl-sys` is empty for the linux target) and nothing uses DTLS.
# Debian ships the fix in 3.0.22-1~deb12u2, but distroless had not rebuilt cc-debian12 yet
# (the latest digest still carried 3.0.20 when this was added on 2026-10-26).
# Re-reviewed 2026-11-18 after the first expiry: cc-debian12:latest is still
# sha256:e5d81ddd… (the pinned digest) and still ships libssl3 3.0.20-1~deb12u2; Cargo.lock
# has no openssl / openssl-sys / native-tls at all. Extended, not fixed.
# On expiry: bump the distroless digest in the four Dockerfiles and drop this entry.
CVE-2026-84782 exp:2026-12-09

# libssl3 3.0.20 (distroless/cc-debian12 base) — DoS via unbounded QUIC frame queueing.
# NOT APPLICABLE: no shipped binary links OpenSSL — `readelf -d` on the four 1.0.4 binaries
# lists only libgcc_s / libm / libc / ld-linux, and Cargo.lock has no openssl / openssl-sys /
# native-tls (TLS is rustls) — and nothing uses OpenSSL's QUIC stack.
# UNFIXED upstream when added on 2026-11-23: trivy reports it `affected` with no fixed version,
# and cc-debian12:latest is still the pinned sha256:e5d81ddd….
# On expiry: re-check Debian/distroless for a fixed libssl3, bump the digest if there is one,
# otherwise re-review and extend.
CVE-2026-107494 exp:2026-12-09
